# v312 — EVENT WORKSPACE (one Event across the company)
#
# APPLICATION-ONLY. This release deploys no database object: no migration, no
# table, no column, no function, no policy, no trigger, no renamed identifier and
# no changed projection contract. event_workspace() is consumed exactly as v309
# and v310 left it, and its envelope version is not bumped.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ANYWAY. Every release from v292a forward declares its
# database prerequisites, so that certification asks "can the database we are
# shipping against run this?" rather than assuming it. v312 declares none of its
# own — it declares the level it requires beneath it, which is v311.
#
# WHAT v312 READS, ALL PRE-EXISTING AND ALREADY CERTIFIED AT v311 OR EARLIER:
#   · engagement_occurrences(p_booking, p_now)   — the Function list, and each
#     Function's execution lineage (event_ref, null where unreleased)
#   · occurrence_profile                          — Function display identity
#   · projection_occurrence_brief(p_occurrence)   — Function facts
#   · event_workspace(p_event)                    — one Function's operational truth
#   · kitchen_event_panel(p_event, p_as_of)       — the v311 Kitchen seam, re-hosted
#
# Each is already declared by the release that introduced it; repeating them here
# would assert v312 as their origin, which it is not. min_release carries the
# prerequisite instead, exactly as v296 — the existing application-only precedent —
# does.
#
# NO PRODUCTION MUTATION IS AUTHORIZED BY THIS ARTIFACT, and no production
# mutation is possible from it: there is nothing to apply.
#
# ROLLBACK. Application-only, so rollback is the application rollback governed by
# SOP Rule 5 — Vercel Instant Rollback to a governed production deployment, or a
# fast-forward of eventcore-production to a prior certified SHA. No database step
# exists to reverse, and none should be invented.
#
# BOOKING CRM IS NOT CONTACTED. Shared Cross-Product Ledger v2, X-013: EventCore
# only — no query, no migration, no synchronization, no comparison, no deployment.
release          v312
migration
migration_source none
min_release      v311
